## Handoff

**Frontend scope for Taiga #12 (due tasks a date) — complete.**

**Files changed:**
- `frontend/src/api.js` — `createTask(title, priority, dueDate)` now sends `due_date` in the POST body; added `setDueDate(id, dueDate)` hitting `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/due-date`.
- `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx` — new `dueDate` state, `<input type="date" className="due-date-input" aria-label="Due date (optional)">` between priority select and Add button; `onAdd(trimmed, priority, dueDate || null)`; resets to `''` after submit.
- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` — added module-level `todayISO()`/`isOverdue(task)` helpers (strict `<` comparison, gated on `!task.done`, per AC5/AC7); `TaskList`/`TaskRow` both gained an `onDueDateChange` prop threaded through exactly like `onPriorityChange`; each row now renders a `.due-date-input` bound to `task.due_date || ''`, a `.due-date-clear` `×` button (only rendered when `task.due_date` is set), and an `.overdue-badge` (`role="status"`, decorative `⚠` marked `aria-hidden`, visible text "Overdue") when `isOverdue(task)` is true.
- `frontend/src/App.jsx` — `AddTask`'s `onAdd` now forwards `dueDate` into `api.createTask`; added `onDueDateChange={(id, dueDate) => run(() => api.setDueDate(id, dueDate))}` passed to `TaskList`.
- `frontend/src/App.css` — added `.due-date-input`, `.due-date-clear` (+ `:hover`), `.overdue-badge` rules verbatim from the design doc; added `flex-wrap: wrap` to `.task` so rows wrap on narrow viewports instead of overflowing with the extra controls.

**Deviations from design:** none — implementation matches `docs/design.md` exactly, including the contrast-checked colours (reused `.error`'s red, no new palette) and the ARIA labeling scheme.

